We are experiencing an interresting problem on 2 of our 7 DEC
5500 servers ( running Ultrix 4.1 ).

Occasionally, ( once every few days to several times a day ) the
system(s) hang for 5-10 minutes.  During this time it is not possible
to login and all jobs appear to stop.  The login sequence gets as far
as asking for the password but stops at that point.  The system(s)
returns to normal after 5-10 minutes.  During the hangs, terminal
activity stops, jobs appears to stop.

The sytems on which we are having problems have ~ 500 meg swap.  The
others have less than 200 meg.

Interresting correlation:

   Monitor ( version V1.3 ) ran very slowly on these 2 machines and
   took as much as 50% of the cpu time.  On the remaining 5 machines
   monitor ran fine ( at about .5% of cpu ).

Experimentation:

   We were experimenting today, and finally decided to try lowering
   the amount of swap space.  One of the machines had a total of ~ 500
   meg of swap.  It was spread across 4 drives, with 2 swap partitions
   on one of the drives.  We configured the system with only 4 swap
   partitions spread across 4 drives ( and equal amount in each
   partition for total of ~250 meg).  Monitor ran just fine on that
   machine at that point.  ( unfortunately, we need to have > 400 meg
   but will live with it like this for a while ).

   So, we decided to try the second machine.  It had a slightly
   different swap configuration: 5 swap partitions of differing sizes
   and 2 on one disk for a total of ~500 meg.  We configured with only
   2 partitions ( one 100 meg and one 400 meg ) on separate drives.
   The slow response of monitor continued.  We then went with 3
   partitions of the same size spread across 3 drives.  That worked
   just fine, with a slight anomaly -- if we configured the 3 swap
   partitions but only came up with one of the swaps enabled ( ie not
   in fstab ), monitor consumed 20-30% of the cpu time.  Swapon of the
   second swap partition reduced the %cpu to 10-15.  Finally adding
   the last partition brought monitor back to its normal operating
   mode ( < .5%).

   We attempted one additional test.  This time we ran with 4 swap
   partitions on 3 drives ( 2 on the last one ), and added them one at
   a time after boot ( swapon ).  Monitor started out at about 15%
   with only 1 swap partition.  Second swap partition brought it to
   25% --- on up toabout 55% with all added.

What is going on?  Who out there is running with larger than 250 meg
swap on dec risc 5500's?  Has anyone else seen at least the monitor
behavior?  It is pretty hard for us to believe this is "normal", or
due to differences in size of the swaps, or even having 2 swaps on one
drive.  We have this configuration on other sun's and ibm rs6000's
without problems.





