I am running a 5820 with about 550 Meg of swap and I had similar
problems with monitor.  The problem really lies with the portion of
the program which is trying to determine what memory is left unused.
Try running /etc/pstat -T and you will see that it will take much longer
the more swap you have.  In my case, the monitor program would not display
anything because the check for memory fragmentation took longer than the
time between refreshes of monitor.  I had to disable that portion of monitor
to get it to run at all!  This is a pretty good indication, by the way,
of how slow the 5820 is when it comes to memory access.

Hope this helps.

