A user writes about a problem with booting RSX11M, in that the boot
sequence ends after the RED command.

It looks like your boot image has not been SAVed. After it does the
RED command, enter the current date and time (just to record the date
and time that the system was SAVed), and enter SAV /WB<cr>.

This will write back the memory image to the boot image with SAV
running, and will, I believe, fix all the other problems you are having.

