From: tihor@acf3.NYU.EDU (Stephen Tihor)
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec
Subject: Re: UPS advice, and how to do a remote shutdown (shutdown from C)?
Message-ID: <23030005@acf3.NYU.EDU>
Date: 7 Aug 91 18:14:00 GMT
References: <1991Aug7.160101.23503@athena.mit.edu>
Sender: notes@cmcl2.nyu.edu (Notes Person)
Organization: New York University
Lines: 27
Nntp-Posting-Host: acf3.nyu.edu

To shutdown a VMS system you will want to run a detached process since the 
shutdown code, by its nature, can not be ru8n successfully from say a batch job.
You want something like the two examples below from our network triggered
over temperature shutdown system.

$!-----------------------------------------------------------
$ SET NOON 	! run detached shutdown process
$ STOP SHUTDOWN
$ RUN/UIC=SYSTEM/INPUT=CLUSTER$MANAGER:DET_SHUTDOWN.COM-
	/PROCESS_NAME="SHUTDOWN" -
	/OUTPUT=SYS$MANAGER:DET_SHUTDOWN.LOG SYS$SYSTEM:LOGINOUT


$!-----------------------------------------------------------
$ set noverify	! Detached shutdown procedure
$ set noon
$ request/to=central "Starting detached shutdown"
$ ! Time reasons spindowndisks sitespecific backup  autoreboot 
$ !		remove_node,reboot
$ if p1 .eqs. "" then p1 = F$STRING(120)
$ reason = "Temperature exceeds safe level in machine room"
$ minutes = F$INTEGER(p1)
$ define shutdown$inform_nodes 'F$GETSYI("SCSNODE")'
$ @sys$system:shutdown 'minutes' "''reason'" NO YES "within half an hour" -
	YES "REMOVE_NODE,REBOOT_CHECK"
!	YES "CLUSTER,REBOOT_CHECK"
$ request/to=central "Detached shutdown aborted?"


