is that the client resource mechanism is broken (you can't specify resources seperately
for different screens).  As one of the people who designed
it wrong, all I can do is apologize, and say it is fixed in MIT X11R5.

The general problem of windows crossing onto multiple screens is more or less
unsurmountable, unless you wish to reduce things to a least common denominator.
Think of the problems of a 32 bit 3D display and a single bit monochrome display
sometime.  The MAC doesn't face as wide a diversity of display types, or attempt
