We have a loaner DECstation 5000/200 running ULTRIX 4.2 (rev 96), here
while we port some software to it.  It came without any paper
documentation, so we're having the grandest time poking around in the
dark.  Perhaps some more frequent ULTRIX programmers would be able to
help with some simple questions:

I tried creating /dev/cua with the same major device number as
/dev/tty00 and the same minor plus 128.  When I try to open it I'm
told there's no such device.  I'm able to go in and out through
/dev/tty00 with no problem, so maybe ULTRIX just doesn't use the
inbound/outbound minor device number pairing scheme.

question 1: What are the ULTRIX conventions regarding naming and
numbering of "ACU" auto-call units?

<sys/ttydev.h> lists speeds up through B9600, then EXTA and EXTB.  The
highest speed entry in /etc/gettytab shows sp#19200.  When I am
talking out through /dev/tty00 and ioctl it to 19200, I can talk to a
modem whose DTE is latched at 19200.  But when I try to use 38400, I
can't talk to that modem with its DTE latched at 38400.  In fact, I
discovered by experimentation that even though I ioctl'd the serial
port to 38400 (EXTB), the modem still hears me talking at 19200.

question 2: How can one use the tty ports (serial async) at 38400?

We formerly had a DECstation 3100, but it didn't have enough lines on
its modular-jack connectors to control a modem, so we then got a 5000,
which has a full standard DB-25 serial interface connector.  We can
plug our modems in with their usual cables.  Now I'd like to use
RTS/CTS flow control, but this is a TERMIO system, right?

question 3: (and perhaps the most lost) How does one use RTS/CTS flow
control under ULTRIX?

Thanks for any suggestions you can offer!


