Please take your snickering elsewhere; you've just been lucky.

As I said, DS5000's with mixtures of MX and CX displays will usually
work, but there is a design flaw with the client resource mechanism
(you can't specify resources on a per-screen basis); this design
flaw doesn't get fixed until X11R5 is available.  Digital does not
formally support mixed configurations as a result of this problem.
Manufacturers who claim to support mixed configurations are letting customers
in for potential problems.  This is as true for Sun hardware as for
Digital hardware, or HP, or IBM, or whomever.  As one of the guilty for
the design mistake, I think I can speak with authority.

This has nothing to do with whether the hardware works (it does, just
plug the board in and reboot your machine), or the server works (it does); 
but your applications may malfunction until this is fixed, if you happen 
to specify colors in an unfortunate way.

For Digital to say something is supported, we believe things should
work sensibly without traps for the unwary, which are certainly
there until R5 is widespread (which it isn't, yet).  
If you've not run into the problem, you've been lucky.  I've
generally been lucky as well, with my .Xdefaults configuration.
But the real solution is "fixed in X11R5".

