A while ago I posted an iquiry about file transfer between PDPs
running TSX-Plus over RT-11 and VAX/VMS, and since I received
twice as much e-mail from people in similar situation to ours
than suggestions about how to do it from people who already
had traveled the streach, here's a summary of the responses.
Thanks to the following for taking their time to help:

	wagner%star@sj.ate.slb.com
	uu.psi.COM!arrent!angel
	<SLSW2@cc.usu.edu>
	<systemm@alhrg.wpafb.af.mil>
	jmorris@math.utexas.edu
	WHD0675@ritvax.isc.rit.edu


and here's what I gathered from their notes, and how we've done so far:

Most seem to relay on a serial link and KERMIT.  A couple of respondents
used the DEC supplied EXCHANGE utility (included with VMS), while others
suggested third party TCP/IP software, and still other's mentioned DECnet.

From our initial tries with EXCHANGE not much good has come out.  I've
used COPY on the PDP to put file onto a 9trk tape which was then mounted
/FOREIGN on VMS level, and then EXCHANGE was invoked.  A "MOUNT tape:"
command from within EXCHANGE would see the tape as DOS-11 format, and
"MOUNT tape:/VOLUME_FORMAT=RT11" would fail with a "parse error" on tape:.
"DIR tape:" would complain about label format (it should... it was mounting
the tape as DOS-11), and mounting the tape with label didn't do much good
either.

On DCL level, the tape could be mounted as FILES-11 (with label), and DIR
showed all files with their right sizes, and they could be copied to disk,
but all files were created empty (size 0/0).

I'll still try EXCHANGE with BUP format tapes, and with a PDP hard drive
mounted foreign directly on the VAX (we use the same controllers on both),
but so far the utility has been a major disapointment.

We'll also try KERMIT (on its way from DECUS), though as the systems
are not in the same location, and are connected with a couple of Telebit
T1600 modems through DLV11 type of controllers (no hardware flow control),
I'll leave that option as a last resort (interactivelly, a ^S/^Q will
miss characters, and that's with max "silo" size, and real-time priority
on the PDP side (I haven't looked what can be done on the VAX side.))

OK, if you still with me and know where I've goofed (and how it can be fixed)
I'd appeciate your comments.

Thanks to all,

-Mariusz
