bonk@Informatik.TU-Muenchen.DE (Thomas Bonk) writes:
>I have a DEC5000/200 running with Ultrix  V4.1 (Rev.52). I expanded the
>machine to 56MByte of physical memory. Before booting the machine knows
>the memory [ ... ]
>But when booting Ultrix knows only 40MBytes:	[ ... ]

This will happen if there are any "holes" in memory, ie, the memory space
is not contiguous.  Ultrix cannot handle noncontiguous memory.

Did you put the new board(s) adjacent to the existing ones?  Try typing:

		>> cnfg 7

This will list all boards in the system by slot and indicate their sizes.
Especially look for board 5, which is the bank containing megs #40-48.

If all boards are adjacent, you may have a memory error.  This would mark
a page as bad in the memory bitmap, and since Ultrix stops at the very
first hole in RAM it would only see memory up to that point.  If you
haven't seen any memory errors in the selftest report, try:

		>> setenv VERBOSE 1
		>> t 7/mem 5

This runs memory tests on board 5, which would probably be the bad one.  If
you omit the `5', memory tests will run on all boards.

Personally, I suspect nonadjacent boards.

Good luck, and please feel free to ask again if none of this helps,

^E (ex-3MAX firmware type)

-- 
