Fellow DECers,
 
We are having some weird problems with DECTerm
and editors that maybe some of you have seen/conquered, etc.

The problem is when users rlogin or telnet to another
UNIX box from within the DECTerm Application.

Under DECTerm, even AFTER we put the vt300 entry in the
termcap (this is on other machines, SUN, HP, etc) vi and
emacs still don't like things. Vi starts in the middle of the screen
and updates only 24 lines, no more. If you exit, setenv TERM
vt100, then you can get screen refreshes for the
full window, but you have to first go down with the cursor
below the 24th line before it fills the window. Things
get MUCH worse if you resize the DECTErm window. Then
EMACS crashes and vi "skips" lines. This even happens
if the "other" machine is a DECStattion!

Emacs is worse, it never fills the window no matter what
you do with setenv or stty (we tried that too).

A printenv shows the machine understands that the telneted or rlogin'd
screen IS a vt100 screen, but the SPARC just won't behave
well. This is the case on DECSTations running Ultrix 4.2
going TO SPARCs, DECS, and HPs runing HP/UX. IBM RS6000 
with AIX did a little
better but those machines have special kernel hacks
that I do not know about (i.e. they're not _vanilla_).

Has anyone else found a way to make the DECTerm windows behave??

Thanks in advance!

--Roger

