Here is a long shot stunt to a long shot problem.
This is tedious but COULD work.
Hook up your VAX and your PDP11 serial port to serial port and use
a null modem to join them.
Then do set host/dte/log=foo.bar txa9 (Let us pretend that txa9 is the
port you are using on the VAX to go through) from the VAX.
You now enter the PDP through a not SO well known terminal emulator.
The good news with this is that all that happends on the PDP will be logged
in the file foo.bar. Now display your documents one by one and you will
capture them on your VAX. Beware though: It is easy to get DATA OVERRUN
so use a slow link and not too much text at a time Buffer size could also
be tinkered with (Say after me: I LOVE my sysgen manual!).
This also works with some versions of Kermit. You then enter "log session"
from inside the Kermit program.
And hey! Desperat people have done much more stupid things than this! :)
The log file on the VAX will be in ascii flavor but COULD need some
converting using FDL or a plain honest editor or program.
All this provided that there is now way to produce ascii files on the PDP.

/L. Persson, Harlosa PD computer centre


