	It probably looks like a VT100-case but has some coloured 
keys on the keyboard. My version was known as a DECmate 1 - 
depends where you look for labels. There was also a workstation 
known as a WS-78 that came on a pedestal stand - suspect it had 
floppies too - also pretty keys.

	If you have a printer built in then you may have the 
VT-52/VT-55 housing with a fast port and screen. Also part of the 
early DEC word processing boxes - probably with a PDP-8 built 
into the back.

	DEC also made a PC called the ROBIN - it had a pair of 
standard-looking 5.25" floppies (ie NOT RX-50s) in a small box.
I am not sure what the screen looked like - I think like a VT100.

	Good luck with the system. I should have some terminal 
software available to talk to an external host - most of them did 
- it is just a matter of finding it.
