>You should order the console cable from Digital (or you can make it yourself
>but I don't remeber the pinouts).

This only works on VAXstations.   The DECstation 2100/3100 requires a
mouse loopback tail and the removal of the video SIMM to run with an
ASCII console.   The DECstation 5000/200 automatically goes to an
ASCII console if no frame buffer is installed on the TurboChannel.

The DECstation 5000/120 should work with an ASCII console just by
connecting the console to the correct port and not installing a frame
buffer.  David Elrod kindly tried this out on one of his DECstation
5000/120s a little while ago, and verified that the ASCII console does
indeed work, and the system comes up single user.  It didn't come up
multi-user, but this was probably because it was configured to run
with a frame buffer.

Disclaimer: just because it works for us doesn't mean that it's
officially supported by DEC.   If you can order it, though, that would
seem to imply that it's supported.

			       _MelloN_


